# Complete Auth Service Implementation Plan

This implementation plan details the technical steps to complete the **Auth Service** microservice (`AUTH-SERVICE`) in `Backend/AUTH-SERVICE` for the **DriveClone** application, adhering strictly to the 16 project specification documents (`api-contracts.md`, `database-schema.md`, `monorepo-structure.md`, `MVPTechDoc(2).md`, etc.).

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Database Auto-DDL vs MySQL DDL Script:** By default, Spring Data JPA `hibernate.ddl-auto: update` is enabled in `application.yml`. On startup, JPA will automatically create `users`, `roles`, `user_roles`, and `refresh_tokens` tables in MySQL (`auth_db`). Additionally, an automated `DataInitializer` bean will seed initial roles (`ROLE_USER`, `ROLE_ADMIN`) into the database if they are absent.
> - **Jakarta Validation Dependency:** We will ensure `spring-boot-starter-validation` is present in `pom.xml` for request validation (`@Valid`, `@NotBlank`, `@Email`).
> - **Error & Response Uniformity:** All API endpoints (`/api/auth/*`) will return the standard envelope structure:
>   `{ "success": boolean, "message": String, "data": Object }`.

